  "introPrivateTitle": "Your files stay on your phone",
  "introPrivateBody": "No account is needed. Share or export only when you choose. The scanner may need internet for its first setup.",
  "privacyBody": "DocScan — current version\n\nYour scanned images, PDFs, document names and preferences are stored locally on this device. DocScan does not upload documents or require an account.\n\nScanning uses Google Play services and the ML Kit document scanner. Its initial component download or update may need internet and is managed by Google Play services. PDF preview and compression run on your device.\n\nSharing and Save to device send a copy only to the app or location you select. Those apps and storage providers have their own privacy practices.\n\nThis development version integrates Google Mobile Ads using Google test ad IDs. The advertising and consent SDKs may connect to Google and process device identifiers, IP address, app interactions and diagnostic information to serve ads, manage privacy choices and prevent fraud. No scanned images, PDFs, names or file paths are passed to the advertising SDK by DocScan. Ad requests are gated by Google UMP consent status. Where required, you can revisit Ad privacy choices in Settings. Ads need internet; scanning and saved files remain available without ads. Premium purchases use Google Play Billing. Google handles payment processing; DocScan does not receive your payment card details. A signed purchase receipt is stored privately on this device for offline ad-free access and checked with Google Play when available. Buying and restoring require Google Play connectivity. No document images, PDFs or names are sent to billing. There is no separate analytics SDK in this version.\n\nDelete documents from the Documents list. Uninstalling removes private app data; exported or shared copies remain in their destination. Android backup is disabled for private app data.\n\nThis offline information page is not a published Play Store privacy policy. A public policy URL and developer contact must be provided before release.",
